   "lectureId": "BRGSA-M01-L01",
   "title": "Lean Validation",
   "text": "Each one feels like rational thinking from inside, but all 3 lead to the same outcome, spending months and money on assumptions that a one-week test could have disproved. The third point is the cost of skipping a lean validation is quantifiable. 6 to 18 months and 20 lakhs to 2 crore to learn what your validation test can do in zero to 10,000 rupees, and maybe in days or weeks. Fourth, always remember lean validation is not market research because market research tells you what people say as their opinions, wherein lean validation tests will actually tell you what people Research focuses on the user's belief or opinions that, \"Okay, this sounds good,\" but the lean validation focuses on the user's real action towards the business idea. Are they clicking? Are they signing up? Are they pre-ordering? These are actual behaviors or the user actions, while the survey responses are simply just opinions. And the fifth, we learned that both Clairo and Zoko have hypothesis that would need structured test and now you have the framework to understand why. Over the next all modules, you will diagnose those tests, interpret the signals, and build a complete growth system on top of a validated foundation. Next topic is smoke test, which is the fastest method for getting a real market signal before even writing a single line of code in building your product or before even building hundreds of business decks on your business idea. That's all for this topic. See you in the next one."
