   "title": "Minimum Viable Product Validation Logic Validation Under Low Resources",
   "text": "functional MVP comes after the 4 signals on the next slide are green, not before that. The 4 signals is like all 4 must be positive before you start building. The signal one is, of course, as we have been talking, does the demand exist? A smoke test or a landing page showed a positive where you had, let's say, 3 signal result, CTR above 3%, sign up rate above 15%, bounce rate below 60%, that means real people engaged with proposition. If there are red, then of course signals were mixed or below threshold. You have to design another experiment, that is what we have already learned. Signal 2, is the commitment, where at least one pre-sales payment or letter of intent or signed deposit was received from a real ICP or a real target customer, and not just an email sign up or a survey. Real commitment with real money or a real bond or signature. If it is red or like you have not achieved this so far, that means you still have only soft interest. Signal 3, is your ICP clarity. Can you name the specific company type, the role in that company, the trigger event on which they will exactly buy your product? Who can be the budget authority? Who will buy first? And all of these particular answers, are you able to answer clearly? If yes, then it's a go ahead. If it is red, then maybe you have still not found the real target audience or the real ICP. You are still either too broad or maybe in the wrong direction."
