   "text": "are most comfortable. So, if you are missing a certain method, on the basis of that, your right tool will exactly be activated. Suppose if you're missing basic demand signal, your smoke test or ad creative where the budget was zero to 3,000, time was 2 to 3 days, a fake LinkedIn post with a, like a Loom link, it costs nothing. If you are missing message resonance, then it is landing page validation where your budget is could be like 1 to 5,000, time 3 to 5 days. You can simply create on a Carrd or a Typedream tool. If you're missing willingness to pay, then you have to focus on pre-sales offer. Again, you can keep zero budget for like 5 to 7 days. You can keep a founding customer offer or like through a founding, like a DM customer campaign, just a LinkedIn account and multiple other things. If you're missing behavioral depth, then maybe you can actually have some test interviews. Again, budget zero, you can build in 1 to 2 weeks. Maybe you can actually have 10 Zoom calls with your real ICPs because it will cost nothing except the time for preparation and engaging with your target customer. Now, if all the 4 signals are positive, then only start building the functional MVP. So, the rule at the bottom, you can see that match the method to the missing signal. Generally, what people do, whatever they are more comfortable, they start choosing that specific tool, which is not the right way of doing that. Now, let's talk about 3 budget tiers."
