   "text": "And the magic is, let's say in the day 21 photo ask. At day 21, Zoko asked the creator for a before and after photo. Now, the creator who actually used the product has one, and that will create the validation. The creators who produce day 21 content are the ones whose audiences trust them on this particular category. And those are the seeds that will compound your growth because then their followers, friends of those followers, friends of friends of those followers, and you will start getting that viral effect. Now, let's talk about the four mistakes that founders might do with this zero-budget traction program. The first is running these 5 levers half-heartedly. That, \"Hey, okay, out of 6, forget about 2, I can run 5 of them.\" But if you'll start running 5, you'll be able to do that half-heartedly because these zerobudget traction compounds with the depth and effort. And if you will actually use 5 levers, then you'll be able to provide only 20% effort at all the 5, and then you might end up with zero result from everywhere. So, pick 2 and commit fully instead of halfbaked commitment. Use ICE scoring framework honestly to decide what to do and what not to do. The second mistake that people do is we have already discussed here in this topic itself that they abandon at week 6. That, hey, nothing is moving. We know that zero budget is a slow start. Weeks 1, through 6, might look nothing, maybe weeks 20 through 26 will start looking like the real success."
