   "text": "The founders who actually win this zero budget traction treat it like the main game and not just as a backup. So, 5 quick takeaways from this topic. The first, the zero budget traction assets compounds avoids you auctions at scale and builds moats that paid channels can never generate. 2, you have the 6 levers built in public, SEO cornerstone, community hosting, viral mechanics, creator seeding, and earned media. Third, you will use the ICE framework to pick the 2 best levers out of this. The ICE framework is impact, confidence, and ease. You just have to score honestly, average them, and rank them. The honest score is what separates this method from just a wishful thinking method. The fourth point is you run and write a very clear 30, 60, and 90 days plan. You set up it, compound it, and then you evaluate it in these 3 different packets of the timeline. You will write the plan before you start, so you can evaluate that against it at the day 90. And the fifth is you avoid the 4 failure"
