   "lectureId": "IBM-M05-L10",
   "title": "SELCO s Sustainable Business Model",
   "text": "He would say that first of all, his engineers, who were also his salespeople, would need to understand the real need of the poor. They were not there to sell them a light. They were there to address their needs. And there were multiple occasions where SELCO figured out that even if a person needed to buy 2 lights, it was enough for the person to buy only 1 light. Hence, he needed his engineers to be very empathetic to the needs of the customer. There was no pressure to sell more. There was no pressure to make money out of the customer, which a typically commercial venture would probably have in their mind. We have discussed in the case study how they would look at the construction of a house and position a light maybe at the intersection of 2 rooms to ensure that the light reaches both the rooms, thus reducing the need for buying more than 1"
