   "title": "Understanding Impact Investment",
   "text": "Hello everyone. My name is Sanchayan Chakraborty. I'm a partner at a firm called Aavishkaar Capital. We do impact investments which is the topic of the lecture today. Impact investment is a 10year-old concept within the world of investments. It is a subset of what is called as alternative investments which includes private equity and venture capital. It grew out of a realization that you can use capital to positively impact society and the climate. There are 3 kinds of players who do impact investment and I will tell you more about each of these, each of these as we go along. These players include some original investors who came up with this concept, which includes Aavishkaar. There are some who are commercial, traditional commercial investors who also realize this is a good opportunity for financial returns while also benefiting society. And the third category includes philanthropic organizations. These are foundations and others who have been funding programs for social good, and they also allocate a portion of their funding now to impact investment. So, what are impact investments? I give you a very brief overview of that. Impact, this is a definition that has been accepted by what is called as Global Impact Investing Network. It is an association of institutions which engage in, in, in impact investing, and it's a widely accepted definition. This definition is on your screen."
