   "text": "this entire business model, especially allowing the ladies and the girls of the village to go and seek employment with RuralShores. And Murali and his team was always very conscious of not to do anything that was against the accepted norms and beliefs of the community. Their center partner model was also quite remarkable because they realized that without local partnership, they will have to make huge investment. And hence, they went out and sought center partners or franchisees so that these people could bring in the investment and also deal with the local administration and infrastructural challenges which could take advantage of local knowledge and local connections. Let us now think about the growth options that we talk in this particular case. How do you think RuralShores could grow their business? The case talks about three possibilities. RuralShores could continue to build centers of their own. RuralShores could follow a center partner model where they encourage a franchisee to replicate their model in some other villages while RuralShores will control the processes, the standards there. And third is about diversification, which in the case is given as business enablement services. While RuralShores were involved in business process outsourcing, could they also become insurance agents for big companies? Because they understand the village, they understand the context, they are familiar with the people around."
