   "text": "Maybe they can use their same connections to sell other products and services. I would want you to think about the pros and cons of each of these three options and tell me which one do you think RuralShores should choose. Let us now discuss about the pros and cons of each of these options. If you build your own center, one of the key advantage is the tight control that you have over quality. You can also sustain the social mission. You can do exactly what you were doing in your earlier centers, train your people similarly, and send them to run those centers. The downside of that is it is expensive. You will need investments, and as a result, it will be slow to develop. You will also not have the local knowledge in other places. You may be familiar with certain conditions in rural Karnataka, but that may be very different from prevailing conditions in rural West Bengal or in rural Gujarat. So, those are some of the challenges of building own centers: high investment, lack of local"
